    "lang": "en",
    "category": "chest",
    "name": "Dumbbell bench press",
    "content": "---\nexercise_name: Dumbbell bench press\nexercise_type: strength\ntags:\n- front_delts\n- shoulders\n- triceps\naliases:\n- Жим гантелей лежа\ncategory: chest\ntier: 5\nrank_source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ykQlXirszbo\nvideo: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=odsAnZIk58k\nhelper_id: 10\n---\n\n# Dumbbell bench press\n\n**Best** · [Chest Exercises Ranked (BEST TO WORST!)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ykQlXirszbo)\n\n**Target muscles:** Pectoralis major, front delts, triceps.\n\n## Starting position\n\nLie on a bench or on the floor (floor press). Take the dumbbells and bend the elbows at 45° to the torso (do not flare the elbows to 90°).\n\n## Step-by-step technique\n\n1. On the exhale, press the dumbbells up powerfully, bringing them together over the center of the chest.\n2. On the inhale, lower the dumbbells under control over 3 seconds.\n3. Pause for 1 second at the bottom, feeling the stretch in the chest muscles.\n\n## Key points\n\n- Your elbows should not flare out to the sides at 90° (a risk to the shoulder joints).\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Letting your shoulder blades come off the bench as you press.\n\n## 🛡️ Spine safety\n\n45° elbows protect the shoulder joints. Do not over-arch the lower back into a powerlifter-style bridge.\n\n## 🛋️ At home, with what you have\n\nWithout a bench, press from the floor (floor press): the floor limits the range of motion and protects the shoulders. Bend the knees so the lower back stays on the floor.\n\n## Video\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=odsAnZIk58k\n"
